WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.234
-Welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:05.267
Thank you for being here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:06.400
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.400
Well, guys, as the
war in Ukraine continues,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.033
a lot more American companies
are distancing themselves

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:12.067
from Russia.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.334
And I mean a lot more.

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:14.734
I mean, one of the
major companies is Starbucks.

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:19.334
They just closed all 130
of their stores over there.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.067
Yeah.
And that was just on one street.

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:23.701
-Wow.

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:26.167
-There's always Dunkin' Donuts,
but Putin was like, "Nyet.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:28.400
That's what America runs on."

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:33.801
And the company that owns
Pizza Hut, KFC, and Taco Bell

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.968
suspended its operations
in Russia.

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:39.300
I had no idea Taco Bell
was popular in Russia.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.601
I guess that explains
why everyone sits

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:41.734
50 feet apart from each other.

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:49.801
How good can
Taco Bell be over there?

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:52.634
It's an American company
making Mexican food in Russia.

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:54.033
You know?

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:57.901
It's like a photo copy of
a photo copy of a photo copy.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.567
And then,
facing growing public pressure,

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:01.567
Papa John's announced that it is

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:04.300
halting all
Russian business operations.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.367
Russians were like,
"Finally, some good news."

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.100
But it's not just restaurants.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.434
Philip Morris, the maker of
Marlboro cigarettes,

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:13.868
just announced plans
to scale down operations.

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:15.868
That's tough, because in Russia,
cigarettes make up

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.767
90% of the food pyramid.

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:24.367
-Potato on top.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.767
-You know you messed up when
even tobacco companies are like,

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:27.801
"We can't be
associated with you.

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:28.801
I'm sorry."

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:31.534
Well, guys, today,
President Biden signed

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:35.133
an executive order to establish
the first-ever strategy

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:38.767
from the federal government
to regulate cryptocurrencies.

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:41.067
I'm just worried now that
the government is involved,

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.901
it'll feel like your
parents joining Facebook.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:46.267
All of a sudden,
it's not cool anymore, yeah.

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:48.000
Biden wants to regulate crypto.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.801
He's even looking into
creating a digital dollar.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.734
It'll look exactly like the
regular dollar bill,

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:54.934
except George Washington will
be replaced with an ape

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:56.634
with sunglasses.

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:02.300
Meanwhile, President Biden
met with business leaders today

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.601
to discuss a microchip shortage.

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:05.934
It's kind of
a complicated subject,

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:08.334
but Biden basically wants
to invest billions of dollars

00:02:08.334 --> 00:02:10.601
in silicon chip production
to make sure America

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:12.801
is leading in the tech sector.

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:13.801
It makes sense
when you think about it.

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:15.133
I mean...

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.634
[ Thinking ] Oh, God,
I should not be talking about

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.100
chip production right now.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.200
What the heck
do I know about chips?

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.400
Uh, they're in
phones, computers.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.567
Maybe Tariq can hop on this.
I got to bail.

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:26.734
But that's just my take.

00:02:26.734 --> 00:02:30.334
I mean, Tariq,
what do you think?

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:35.400
-Oh, well, when you take
a look at the issue of, say,

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.734
technological sovereignty,
that we're clearly --

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:40.000
I mean, we're heading to
a dip in the chips --

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.267
[ Thinking ] A dip in the chips?

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:44.367
What the hell
am I talking about?

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:47.334
Jimmy told me we were just
going to play charades today.

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:49.200
I'm not qualified
to talk about this.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.133
Oh, I know.
I'll pass it to Higgins.

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:53.834
He reads up on this stuff.

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:55.667
It's actually all theoretical.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:58.501
Yo, Higgins, did you have
any thoughts on microchips?

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:00.334
-Well, you know, on the
one hand, you obviously have to

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:01.367
account for the differences...

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.767
[ Thinking ] Aw, crap!

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:04.534
I thought they were
talking about potato chips

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:06.067
this whole time.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:10.133
Hmm. I don't do Ruffles because
they hurt the roof of my mouth,

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:13.100
but they are
the best for dipping.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.334
Oh, I can't make up my mind!

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:18.601
-[ Thinking ] What I do is,
I dip one end of the chip

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:20.567
in one dip and one end
in another dip.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.634
Double dip, same chip.

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:25.267
-[ Thinking ] Me? But I don't
know if I even want dip.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:28.033
Straight chip, no dip, baby.

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:31.834
-And that's why I like to say,
"Straight dip, no chip."

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:34.000
Mmm!
-Ew! -- Hig-- Oh, thank you.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.200
Ugh!

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:39.334
Alright, that's good.
Stop, stop, stop, stop.

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:42.100
-Mmm!
-Thank you. Thank you, Higgins.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.200
We got to the bottom of that.
-So warm.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.634
-Appreciate it. Thank you.

00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:46.767
Guys, get this.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.667
I read that Tinder
is now offering

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:51.968
criminal background checks
on potential dates.

00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:55.467
Users heard
and were like, "Wait.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:58.067
You weren't already doing that?
What's going on?"

00:03:58.067 --> 00:03:59.434
So now you get
a message that says,

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:02.300
"You've matched with John,
who's wanted in 46 states."

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:05.067
You go, "Cool. People like him."

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:06.300
And, finally,
did you guys see this?

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.334
Florida was hit with
some major rain this week,

00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:10.601
and it made Disney World flood.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:11.601
Take a look at this.

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:21.067
Yeah. Right away,
Disney sprang into action

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:24.033
by charging guests
50 bucks for a poncho.

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:29.100
It's like a dry-cleaning bag
with Mickey's head on it, yeah.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.133
Disney tried
to play it off like,

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:31.467
"This is just our
newest attraction --

00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:32.467
"Formerly Frozen."

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:33.467
We have a great show.

